// APNT shielded pool v1: the pool-coin covenant (task 3.4).
//
// Target: protocol-design, "Settlement
// and the proof verdict"; specs/apnt-pool-settlement-custody/spec.md, "Pool
// state changes only under the settlement authority".
//
// Maturity: new. Deterministic local-VM evidence only
// (packages/reference-aggregator/test/apnt_pool_settlement_covenant_v1_local_vm.test.ts).
// Not deployed, not frozen, not a chain claim.
//
// A pool coin is a keyless, token-free UTXO under this lock holding pooled
// BCH. Pool coins are interchangeable: nothing on them names a note, owner or
// action. This covenant admits a spend only under the settlement authority:
//
//   authority   input 0 carries a verdict-category token with no capability
//               (a 32-byte category, no capability byte) and is under the pool
//               settlement lock.
//
// Everything else is the settlement covenant's (checks 5 and 7): it sums
// every input under this lock and requires the pool-coin outputs after the
// withdrawals to carry exactly Σ in + Σ deposit − Σ withdrawal − Σ fee,
// token-free. So a settlement can use any pool coins, and can be rebuilt
// around a pool coin another settlement spent first, with the same proof and
// signatures.
//
// This lock embeds the settlement lock, so the settlement lock cannot embed
// this one (P2SH32 hashes would be circular). The settlement covenant instead
// derives this lock at run time from its own locking bytecode and its own
// token category, byte for byte:
//
//   redeem = PREFIX ‖ settlement lock ‖ MIDDLE ‖ verdict category ‖ TAIL
//          = 0x23 ‖ L (35 B) ‖ 0x20 ‖ V (32 B) ‖ TAIL
//
// which is why the two constants are pushed first and the checks follow.
// The builder (apnt_pool_settlement_covenant_v1.ts) reads PREFIX, MIDDLE and
// TAIL from this source's compiled bytes, so the two cannot drift apart.
//
// Unlocking data: the P2SH32 redeem push only.
//
// `//@check NAME` … `//@end` mark one covenant check; the local-VM tests remove
// one at a time (replacing it with its `//@ablated` text), which keeps the
// redeem's PREFIX ‖ L ‖ MIDDLE ‖ V shape.
//
// Local VM acceptance is not chain validation, proof verification, wallet
// acceptance or spendability.

@SETTLEMENT_LOCK_PUSH@ @VERDICT_CATEGORY_PUSH@
// Stack: L V.

// Settlement authority: input 0 holds a verdict-category token with no
// capability ...
//@check AUTH_CATEGORY
<0> OP_UTXOTOKENCATEGORY OP_EQUALVERIFY
//@ablated OP_DROP
//@end
// ... under the pool settlement lock.
//@check AUTH_LOCK
<0> OP_UTXOBYTECODE OP_EQUAL
//@ablated OP_DROP <1>
//@end
